# Matome Foundations — Design-System Catalog (drift guard)

```elixir
# Kino ships with Livebook; no Mix.install needed.
alias Kino.HTML
```

## What this is

A **dev-only** visual catalog of the Matome foundations tokens, rendered
server-side so the `/admin` back-office design system can be eyeballed against
the Flutter client.

**Drift-guard chain:**

```
apps/flutter/lib/core/theme/app_theme.dart   ← single source of truth
        │  (hand-maintained, line-ref'd)
        ▼
services/api/assets/css/foundations.css       ← this notebook renders THIS file
        │
        ▼
apps/flutter_widgetbook/lib/foundations_stories.dart  ← Flutter's live render
```

This notebook reads `assets/css/foundations.css` **at runtime** (it does not
re-declare any values), so it can never drift from the token file. To check for
drift vs Flutter, put this catalog next to the widgetbook Foundations pages
(Colors / Typography / Icons) and compare swatch-for-swatch, both in Light and
Dark.

> ### Threat model (read before running)
>
> Livebook executes **arbitrary Elixir** with the full privileges of the OS
> user. It is the keys-to-the-kingdom by design — great for dev, unacceptable
> in prod. It is therefore **never a dependency of the app and never mounted**
> by the Phoenix router/endpoint. Run it standalone, dev-only:
> `livebook server` then open this file. See
> `docs/livebook-threat-model.md`.

## Load the token file

```elixir
# __DIR__ is services/api/notebooks; the tokens live one level up under assets.
css_path = Path.expand("../assets/css/foundations.css", __DIR__)
css = File.read!(css_path)
IO.puts("Loaded #{byte_size(css)} bytes from #{css_path}")
```

## Colors — every MatomeColors field, Light + Dark

The swatch backgrounds are `var(--matome-*)`, resolved by the injected token
file. Left column is Light (`:root`), right is Dark (`.dark`). Order matches
`foundations_stories.dart`'s `_ColorTokens` list.

```elixir
color_tokens = [
  "primary", "accent", "accent-dark", "accent-soft", "on-accent",
  "background", "surface", "border", "subtle-fill", "subtle-fill-strong",
  "text-primary", "text-secondary", "text-muted", "on-text-primary", "failed",
  "badge-work", "badge-work-text", "badge-personal", "badge-ideas", "badge-default",
  "space-gold", "space-green", "space-blue", "space-orange",
  "space-rose", "space-purple", "space-teal", "space-red"
]

swatches = fn ->
  for t <- color_tokens, into: "" do
    """
    <figure style="margin:0;width:120px">
      <div style="height:56px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--matome-border);
                  background:var(--matome-#{t})"></div>
      <figcaption style="font:600 12px/1.25 var(--matome-font-body);
                  color:var(--matome-text-muted);margin-top:6px">#{t}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    """
  end
end

grid = fn label, theme_class ->
  """
  <section class="#{theme_class}" style="background:var(--matome-background);
           padding:24px;border-radius:16px">
    <h3 style="font:700 24px/1.16 var(--matome-font-display);
        color:var(--matome-text-primary);margin:0 0 16px">#{label}</h3>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px">#{swatches.()}</div>
  </section>
  """
end

HTML.new("""
<style>#{css}</style>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px">
  #{grid.("Light", "")}
  #{grid.("Dark", "dark")}
</div>
""")
```

## Typography — the AppTypography scale

```elixir
type_styles = [
  {"display", "44px", "700", "1.04", "-1px", "font-display"},
  {"title", "24px", "700", "1.16", "-0.4px", "font-display"},
  {"body", "16px", "400", "1.5", "0", "font-body"},
  {"bodySmall", "14px", "400", "1.45", "0", "font-body"},
  {"label", "12px", "600", "1.25", "0.4px", "font-body"}
]

rows =
  for {name, size, weight, line, track, family} <- type_styles, into: "" do
    """
    <div style="padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--matome-border)">
      <div style="font:600 12px/1.25 var(--matome-font-body);
           color:var(--matome-text-muted)">#{name} · #{size} · w#{weight}</div>
      <div style="font-family:var(--matome-#{family});font-size:#{size};
           font-weight:#{weight};line-height:#{line};letter-spacing:#{track};
           color:var(--matome-text-primary)">The quick brown fox</div>
    </div>
    """
  end

HTML.new("""
<style>#{css}</style>
<section style="background:var(--matome-surface);padding:24px;border-radius:16px">
  #{rows}
</section>
""")
```

## Spacing — the AppSpacing scale

```elixir
spacing = ["xxs", "xs", "sm", "md", "lg", "xl", "xxl"]

bars =
  for s <- spacing, into: "" do
    """
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:8px">
      <code style="width:40px;font:600 12px var(--matome-font-body);
            color:var(--matome-text-muted)">#{s}</code>
      <div style="height:16px;width:var(--matome-space-#{s});
           background:var(--matome-accent);border-radius:4px"></div>
    </div>
    """
  end

HTML.new("""
<style>#{css}</style>
<section style="background:var(--matome-surface);padding:24px;border-radius:16px">
  #{bars}
</section>
""")
```

## Icons — app iconography inventory

Icons are **Flutter Material glyphs** (`Icons.*`) and render in the Flutter
widgetbook; the server has no Material icon font, so this catalog carries the
**name inventory** for cross-checking (curated from `apps/flutter/lib` in
`foundations_stories.dart`'s `_appIcons`). Any add/remove there should be
reflected in the widgetbook — this list is the audit anchor.

```elixir
app_icons = ~w(
  inbox_outlined inbox calendar_today_outlined calendar_today
  description_outlined description contacts_outlined contacts folder_outlined
  folder folder_open_outlined workspaces_outlined mic_none_rounded
  mic_none_outlined mic mic_off image_outlined broken_image_outlined
  insert_drive_file_outlined picture_as_pdf_outlined text_snippet_outlined
  slideshow_outlined notes_outlined cloud_done_outlined cloud_sync_outlined
  cloud_off_outlined cloud_off person_outline person_add_alt_outlined
  people_outline groups_outlined business_outlined add
  add_photo_alternate_outlined edit_outlined ios_share share_outlined
  delete_outline drive_file_move_outlined merge_outlined archive_outlined
  download_outlined upload_file_outlined attach_file copy_outlined more_horiz
  play_arrow_rounded pause stop close check arrow_back chevron_right
  expand_more unfold_more search refresh schedule place_outlined auto_awesome
  settings_outlined warning_amber_rounded error_outline grid_view_outlined
  table_rows_outlined
)

tiles =
  for name <- app_icons, into: "" do
    """
    <code style="display:inline-block;padding:6px 10px;margin:4px;border-radius:8px;
          background:var(--matome-subtle-fill);border:1px solid var(--matome-border);
          font:12px var(--matome-font-body);color:var(--matome-text-primary)">#{name}</code>
    """
  end

HTML.new("""
<style>#{css}</style>
<section style="background:var(--matome-surface);padding:24px;border-radius:16px">
  <p style="font:600 12px var(--matome-font-body);color:var(--matome-text-muted)">
    #{length(app_icons)} glyphs in active use</p>
  #{tiles}
</section>
""")
```
